---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LeadForm from '../../components/LeadForm.astro';
import { STICKY_RAK } from '../../data/sticky-cta';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Invest in Ras Al Khaimah Property: Wynn Corridor Shortlist"
  description="RAK property shortlist: Al Marjan, Al Hamra, Mina Al Arab. Pre-Wynn 2027 entry, freehold, Golden Visa AED 2M. Independent Gulf research."
  stickyCta={STICKY_RAK}
>
  <section class="site-container py-12 md:py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <span class="badge-pill mb-4">Ras Al Khaimah</span>
      <h1 class="mb-4">Invest in Ras Al Khaimah property</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
        Beach-resort pricing below Dubai Marina with Wynn Al Marjan catalyst (2027). We filter branded residences and mature communities.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose mb-10">
      <p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Freehold in Al Marjan, Al Hamra, Mina Al Arab. Model net yield carefully, listing gross can exceed VPI-based indices. See our RAK yield methodology before buying.</p>
      <p><a href="/guides/ras-al-khaimah-property-investment-guide/">RAK investment guide</a> · <a href="/guides/al-marjan-island-property-investment/">Al Marjan area guide</a></p>

      <h2>Why RAK is being repriced</h2>
      <p>
        The Wynn Al Marjan Island resort, due to open in 2027, has pulled a wave of branded residence launches onto a small island market. One-bedroom apartments on Al Marjan that traded around AED 550,000 to 900,000 before the announcement now commonly ask AED 900,000 to 1.6 million, a move of roughly 40% to 60% in eighteen months. That is the opportunity and the risk in the same sentence: a large share of investor value is now tied to one island and one event.
      </p>
      <p>
        Underwrite the timeline pessimistically. A twelve-month slip on the resort opening is survivable on a five to seven year hold and fatal on a two-year flip, because the secondary market in RAK is materially thinner than Dubai's and a quick exit can take considerably longer than the same unit would in Marina.
      </p>

      <h2>Three communities, three different bets</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Al Marjan Island.</strong> The launch zone and the Wynn-adjacent play. Highest price movement, highest concentration risk, and the deepest branded-residence pipeline including Mondrian, Waldorf Astoria and Nikki Beach product.</li>
        <li><strong>Al Hamra Village.</strong> The mature alternative: established rents, golf and marina amenity, published service-charge history, and a genuine resale record. Lower headline growth, materially more evidence.</li>
        <li><strong>Mina Al Arab.</strong> Single-developer lagoon community from RAK Properties, which reduces delivery fragmentation but concentrates counterparty risk in one balance sheet.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Getting the yield right</h2>
      <p>
        RAK listing gross yields of 7% to 9% are commonly quoted, above the Dubai average of 5% to 7%. The gap narrows once real costs apply. Service charges on island stock run in the AED 14 to 20 per square foot range, management on a remote-owned unit takes 5% to 10%, and vacancy in a growing phase should be modelled at 10% to 12% rather than the 4% to 6% a mature Dubai building supports. Net frequently lands between 3% and 5%.
      </p>
      <p>
        Listing-based gross and valuation-based indices can diverge sharply here, so treat any single-source yield figure as a claim rather than as evidence. The <a href="/guides/rak-rental-yield-guide/">RAK rental yield guide</a> sets out the method we use.
      </p>

      <h2>Before you reserve</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Confirm the escrow account named in the SPA matches the RAK authority record.</li>
        <li>Ask for the service-charge schedule in AED per square foot, in writing, for the specific tower.</li>
        <li>Check what share of the payment plan falls due at handover; 40% to 60% is common and needs a financing plan.</li>
        <li>Model the exit window at 2029 to 2030 rather than assuming a pre-completion assignment.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Background reading: <a href="/guides/wynn-al-marjan-island-property-impact/">Wynn Al Marjan property impact</a> and <a href="/compare/ras-al-khaimah-vs-dubai-investment/">RAK versus Dubai</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <LeadForm title="RAK property shortlist" subtitle="Al Marjan · Al Hamra · Mina Al Arab" context="Invest RAK property landing" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
